  "notes": "Built from the archived 2023-24 bulletin (fetched raw HTML directly, cross-checked against its own printed Suggested Academic Plan subtotals, which sum to its own stated 'Total Credits 120'). Requirements for the Major section (Prescribed Courses GLIS 101N/102N/400Y, 6cr beyond-level-12/second-language requirement, 21cr Pathway courses with 15cr in one concentration + 6cr from others + 12cr at 400-level-or-higher) is confirmed byte-identical to the 2026 edition -- no real major-requirement change. 2023-24 is the first archived edition on the reformed post-Fall-2023 General Education model (Foundations GQ 6cr/GWS 9cr unchanged, but Knowledge Domains dropped to 3cr each plus a separate 6cr Inter-Domain and 9cr Exploration category) -- this matches the gen_ed tag structure the 2026 file already carries, confirmed by diffing the archived 2022-23 and 2023-24 pages directly (2022-23 still has the old 6/6/6/9-credit-domain model; this file's sibling GLISBA-2022.json documents that difference). One real, verified terminology difference from 2026: 2023-24 still uses 'Foreign Language'/'second foreign language' and 'Other Cultures' wording (renamed to 'World Language'/'World Cultures' starting the 2024-25 edition) -- relabeled the corresponding slot labels below to match. The 2023-24 Suggested Academic Plan is still a single combined 'University Park Campus and Commonwealth Campuses' 8-semester table (120 total credits, no LA 83/LA 283 items) -- the UP/Commonwealth split with LA 83/LA 283 (1.5cr advising-seminar items each) doesn't appear until the 2025-26 edition, so this plan (like the 2026 file, which also omits LA 83/LA 283 entirely) needs no such items. Global Conflict Pathway substitute courses (PLSC 14, GEOG 126, HIST 120/420, PLSC 414, PLSC 458, PLSC 437, CMLIT 449, COMM 410) are not named in the bulletin's own Suggested Academic Plan (only generic 'Major Course from List' / '4XX Level Major Course' placeholders are printed there, since the real departmental Pathway list is not published in the bulletin) -- carried over from the 2026 file's own curatorial pick after confirming each exact course code existed in both the 2022-23 and 2024-25 university-course-descriptions catalogs (bracketing this 2023-24 year), giving high confidence they were unchanged in between rather than assumed.",
